# Branch source of truth

Before starting a new feature, gate, fix, or other independent change:

1. Ensure the current worktree is clean and prior work is committed.
2. Fetch `origin` and confirm the prior pull request is merged when the new work depends on it.
3. Switch to local `main`.
4. Update it from `origin/main` using fast-forward-only pull.
5. Create a fresh, purpose-named branch from that updated `main`.

Do not stack a new change on an unmerged feature branch. Continue on the existing branch only when
the work belongs to the same pull request.
